(6543472, 973263, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real, probably. Shadows on the upper turtle''s claws seem off. Fun, funky image. I like it!</td>', 'Not real, probably. Shadows on the upper turtle''s claws seem off. Fun, funky image. I like it!', '2011-09-17 19:29:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543473, 973441, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real, probably. Hair looks just a little off.</td>', 'Not real, probably. Hair looks just a little off.', '2011-09-17 19:30:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543474, 972565, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real. Curiously, the blown sky adds to the reality of this. Great concept.</td>', 'Not real. Curiously, the blown sky adds to the reality of this. Great concept.', '2011-09-17 19:31:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543475, 973503, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real but well done. Love how you''ve blended the pattern in the sky. What''s the girl standing on?</td>', 'Not real but well done. Love how you''ve blended the pattern in the sky. What''s the girl standing on?', '2011-09-17 19:32:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543476, 973509, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real, but very very well done. Hair is a little too perfect. Light and shadow blending is convincing.</td>', 'Not real, but very very well done. Hair is a little too perfect. Light and shadow blending is convincing.', '2011-09-17 19:34:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543477, 973392, 18197, '<td valign="top">Real, probably. Nice example of high key.</td>', 'Real, probably. Nice example of high key.', '2011-09-17 19:34:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543480, 973555, 18778, '<td valign="top">Two mirror/ interesting reflection images in this challenge!  I''m voting p.shopped on this one.  Perhaps it''s my monitor, but there seems to be a difference in the two shades of red &amp; the gent''s jacket has super sharp edges. But an interesting concept...</td>', 'Two mirror/ interesting reflection images in this challenge!  I''m voting p.shopped on this one.  Perhaps it''s my monitor, but there seems to be a difference in the two shades of red & the gent''s jacket has super sharp edges. But an interesting concept...', '2011-09-17 19:38:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543483, 973116, 18778, '<td valign="top">I''m voting pshop on this one!</td>', 'I''m voting pshop on this one!', '2011-09-17 19:39:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543484, 972811, 18197, '<td valign="top">Real, probably. Shadows feel a little off. Changing my mind - not real. Composit the sigh and background with a different foreground trail?</td>', 'Real, probably. Shadows feel a little off. Changing my mind - not real. Composit the sigh and background with a different foreground trail?', '2011-09-17 19:39:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543486, 972855, 18778, '<td valign="top">A very striking image- I''m guessing P.Shop</td>', 'A very striking image- I''m guessing P.Shop', '2011-09-17 19:39:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543487, 973317, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real, probably.</td>', 'Not real, probably.', '2011-09-17 19:39:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543488, 973577, 18197, '<td valign="top">Real probably ... nice idea well executed.</td>', 'Real probably ... nice idea well executed.', '2011-09-17 19:40:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543489, 973476, 18778, '<td valign="top">Great concept.  On thumbnail alone, it was  one of my faves.  What answers the question of ''is it really inside the bottle'' is the shadows under the car.  P''Shop!?</td>', 'Great concept.  On thumbnail alone, it was  one of my faves.  What answers the question of ''is it really inside the bottle'' is the shadows under the car.  P''Shop!?', '2011-09-17 19:41:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543490, 973451, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real ... angle of the table seems out of kilter with the background/</td>', 'Not real ... angle of the table seems out of kilter with the background/', '2011-09-17 19:41:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543491, 973585, 18778, '<td valign="top">A beautiful, crisp image.  I can ''feel'' how soft the cat is!  I''m guessing the bee is P''shop...</td>', 'A beautiful, crisp image.  I can ''feel'' how soft the cat is!  I''m guessing the bee is P''shop...', '2011-09-17 19:42:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543493, 973474, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real, unless they''ve changed the laws of optics.  Nice concept well executed. It would be fun to see the image in the mirror flipped ... still showing her back but with left and right reversed.</td>', 'Not real, unless they''ve changed the laws of optics.  Nice concept well executed. It would be fun to see the image in the mirror flipped ... still showing her back but with left and right reversed.', '2011-09-17 19:43:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543494, 972844, 18197, '<td valign="top">Real - display window?</td>', 'Real - display window?', '2011-09-17 19:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543495, 973003, 18197, '<td valign="top">It looks so bizarre it is probably real. I know flamingos have teeth and this looks like a photo I saw once of a flamingo at the San Diego zoo. Could it be the same bird?</td>', 'It looks so bizarre it is probably real. I know flamingos have teeth and this looks like a photo I saw once of a flamingo at the San Diego zoo. Could it be the same bird?', '2011-09-17 19:46:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543496, 973386, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real - unless the kid is a cutout. Changing my mind real. Nice work on the shadows.</td>', 'Not real - unless the kid is a cutout. Changing my mind real. Nice work on the shadows.', '2011-09-17 19:48:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543497, 973613, 18778, '<td valign="top">Great job on this.  I''ve been looking at it for a long while &amp; I''ve decided... Paul Revere, The Tattoo Apprentice &amp; the Religious Right man are all P.shop?  Ok, maybe not. But defo the Religious Right Man? I''m really not sure.  But I do love that Captain America took the time to take some pics with the kiddos ;)</td>', 'Great job on this.  I''ve been looking at it for a long while & I''ve decided... Paul Revere, The Tattoo Apprentice & the Religious Right man are all P.shop?  Ok, maybe not. But defo the Religious Right Man? I''m really not sure.  But I do love that Captain America took the time to take some pics with the kiddos ;)', '2011-09-17 19:48:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543499, 973473, 18197, '<td valign="top">If not real, you did a good job with PS.</td>', 'If not real, you did a good job with PS.', '2011-09-17 19:48:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543501, 972749, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real. Nice bubble work.</td>', 'Not real. Nice bubble work.', '2011-09-17 19:49:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543502, 973417, 18197, '<td valign="top">Real ... or at least it started out that way. Like the shape.</td>', 'Real ... or at least it started out that way. Like the shape.', '2011-09-17 19:50:37.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(6543506, 973449, 125275, '<td valign="top">Nicely done. Very ethereal. I''m assuming this is real although certain aspects of the processing are catching my eye, mainly your right hand... If I could figure out exactly what was making me curious about it, I''d probably figure out that it was nothing. :-D<br/> <br/>I''m wondering if this is just your processing style. Some kind of noise reduction or something making me think too hard.<br/> <br/>Still, nice image and we''ll probably see this at the top!</td>', 'Nicely done. Very ethereal. I''m assuming this is real although certain aspects of the processing are catching my eye, mainly your right hand... If I could figure out exactly what was making me curious about it, I''d probably figure out that it was nothing. :-D I''m wondering if this is just your processing style. Some kind of noise reduction or something making me think too hard. Still, nice image and we''ll probably see this at the top!', '2011-09-17 19:52:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543507, 973317, 125275, '<td valign="top">Perfectly shot and executed. This is one for the books. Reminds me of Three Worlds by Escher. I definitely believe there is some compositing going on here, but it''s very unique and very well done.</td>', 'Perfectly shot and executed. This is one for the books. Reminds me of Three Worlds by Escher. I definitely believe there is some compositing going on here, but it''s very unique and very well done.', '2011-09-17 19:53:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543511, 973604, 125275, '<td valign="top">This is cool and definitely heavily photoshopped. I think the lighting on the track is slightly different. That doesn''t seem to be real world shading and light variation on the underside of the train and top side of the track. The track seems to be lit uniformly no matter how far under the body of the train it is. My guess is the "smoke" is some sort of mask. And the lights were added in PP. I''m assuming this is a model train of some kind? Cool shot, nevertheless, and I think it''ll be a top finisher.</td>', 'This is cool and definitely heavily photoshopped. I think the lighting on the track is slightly different. That doesn''t seem to be real world shading and light variation on the underside of the train and top side of the track. The track seems to be lit uniformly no matter how far under the body of the train it is. My guess is the "smoke" is some sort of mask. And the lights were added in PP. I''m assuming this is a model train of some kind? Cool shot, nevertheless, and I think it''ll be a top finisher.', '2011-09-17 19:53:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543512, 973597, 125275, '<td valign="top">Very nice. This is reallly great compositing work. I might sugggest cleaning up some of the "identifying marks" in the extra digit. For example, change the pattterns of the hair or skin using the clone stamp toool. I do see a bit of transparency/soft edge near the wrist, but loooking at the transition on the back of the hand where where it would normallly end, the extra digit is composited *very* realisticallly.</td>', 'Very nice. This is reallly great compositing work. I might sugggest cleaning up some of the "identifying marks" in the extra digit. For example, change the pattterns of the hair or skin using the clone stamp toool. I do see a bit of transparency/soft edge near the wrist, but loooking at the transition on the back of the hand where where it would normallly end, the extra digit is composited *very* realisticallly.', '2011-09-17 19:54:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543514, 973613, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real - probably. Or if real, showing some post processing artifacts.</td>', 'Not real - probably. Or if real, showing some post processing artifacts.', '2011-09-17 19:54:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543517, 973555, 18197, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done!</td>', 'Beautifully done!', '2011-09-17 19:55:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543518, 973225, 18197, '<td valign="top">Perhaps each side is real.</td>', 'Perhaps each side is real.', '2011-09-17 19:55:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543519, 973509, 125275, '<td valign="top">Nicely done. I think you might see the front page with this one. Now, I definitely think it''s composited, mainly because of the way her hair and skirt are falling; they seem to be pressed to the ground (gravity) as opposed to floating. Also, as my wife pointed out, where are the bubbles from her feet coming from? Also, I think the color matching is very well done, she really seems to be lit from inside the tank. It is a bit revealing to me, however, that she seems to be lit *as well* from her head to her feet; as in, the natural fall off of light in water (which is more than in air) does not seem to be affecting her. <br/>Plus I know you wouldn''t want to risk damaging all that coral! :) Still, extremely nice photoshop work. Like I said, I think we''ll see this on the front page.</td>', 'Nicely done. I think you might see the front page with this one. Now, I definitely think it''s composited, mainly because of the way her hair and skirt are falling; they seem to be pressed to the ground (gravity) as opposed to floating. Also, as my wife pointed out, where are the bubbles from her feet coming from? Also, I think the color matching is very well done, she really seems to be lit from inside the tank. It is a bit revealing to me, however, that she seems to be lit *as well* from her head to her feet; as in, the natural fall off of light in water (which is more than in air) does not seem to be affecting her. Plus I know you wouldn''t want to risk damaging all that coral! :) Still, extremely nice photoshop work. Like I said, I think we''ll see this on the front page.', '2011-09-17 19:55:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543524, 973519, 125275, '<td valign="top">So wonderful. I''m in awe of the beauty in this shot. I do think it''s real. What''s interesting about long exposures of water is you begin to see reflections that aren''t there in person, in this case, the reflection of the aurora. Really pretty shot.</td>', 'So wonderful. I''m in awe of the beauty in this shot. I do think it''s real. What''s interesting about long exposures of water is you begin to see reflections that aren''t there in person, in this case, the reflection of the aurora. Really pretty shot.', '2011-09-17 19:56:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543525, 973422, 125275, '<td valign="top">Real. Fake. No, real. Ok, not a real see through laptop, but a well done creation of that illusion. You lined these up really well.</td>', 'Real. Fake. No, real. Ok, not a real see through laptop, but a well done creation of that illusion. You lined these up really well.', '2011-09-17 19:56:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543526, 973010, 18197, '<td valign="top">Probably real.</td>', 'Probably real.', '2011-09-17 19:56:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543527, 972749, 125275, '<td valign="top">Definitely digitally manufactured, but well done. Also, if that bubble over her eye was not added in PP then it''s really good timing on that capture.<br/>My only technical suggestion is to notice how clear the other bubbles are and how cloudy the heart bubble is. If you used the lens flare tool, I''d suggest maybe trying to clone an actual reflection from another bubble. I think it''d come out sharper that way. Still, nicely done and great idea.</td>', 'Definitely digitally manufactured, but well done. Also, if that bubble over her eye was not added in PP then it''s really good timing on that capture.My only technical suggestion is to notice how clear the other bubbles are and how cloudy the heart bubble is. If you used the lens flare tool, I''d suggest maybe trying to clone an actual reflection from another bubble. I think it''d come out sharper that way. Still, nicely done and great idea.', '2011-09-17 19:56:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543528, 973010, 125275, '<td valign="top">Heavy processing, perhaps some tone-mapping? It''s not overdone. <br/> <br/>I''m having a hard time determining if that fly is real. If you put that in there, then it is a really good composite. Final answer: real.</td>', 'Heavy processing, perhaps some tone-mapping? It''s not overdone.  I''m having a hard time determining if that fly is real. If you put that in there, then it is a really good composite. Final answer: real.', '2011-09-17 19:56:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543529, 973382, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real but I love the surreal composition and elements and you''ve put them together beautifully.</td>', 'Not real but I love the surreal composition and elements and you''ve put them together beautifully.', '2011-09-17 19:57:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543530, 973600, 125275, '<td valign="top">I like the long exposure. It''s like the ocean is remembering the surfer. Very dreamy. My verdict is real.</td>', 'I like the long exposure. It''s like the ocean is remembering the surfer. Very dreamy. My verdict is real.', '2011-09-17 19:57:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543531, 973557, 125275, '<td valign="top">This processing is very <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=114969" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Gyaban</a>-esque. Nice strong complementary colors. Were you inspired by <a href="//www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-464768/Thousands-rubber-ducks-land-British-shores-15-year-journey.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a>? I have yet to see an infinite pond so my judgement is digitally manufactured.</td>', 'This processing is very  Gyaban-esque. Nice strong complementary colors. Were you inspired by this? I have yet to see an infinite pond so my judgement is digitally manufactured.', '2011-09-17 19:57:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543532, 973273, 125275, '<td valign="top">This is a very cool image. Dark and ominous. I''m going to say this is a real statue with some texture overlays. I might be wrong about that, and I''d be glad either way. It''s a neat image.</td>', 'This is a very cool image. Dark and ominous. I''m going to say this is a real statue with some texture overlays. I might be wrong about that, and I''d be glad either way. It''s a neat image.', '2011-09-17 19:57:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543533, 973271, 125275, '<td valign="top">Wow. Cool shot. I think you got a good perspective on this that makes it look like there is a ship where there is not supposed to be a ship. I do, however, believe this is real.</td>', 'Wow. Cool shot. I think you got a good perspective on this that makes it look like there is a ship where there is not supposed to be a ship. I do, however, believe this is real.', '2011-09-17 19:57:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543534, 973545, 125275, '<td valign="top">Very pretty. I think the moon was added or altered in PP. If you used a big zoom lens to make it look bigger, you wouldn''t have gotten so many stars. Real or not it''s a very pretty shot.</td>', 'Very pretty. I think the moon was added or altered in PP. If you used a big zoom lens to make it look bigger, you wouldn''t have gotten so many stars. Real or not it''s a very pretty shot.', '2011-09-17 19:57:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543535, 972844, 125275, '<td valign="top">My guess is that this is a composite of at least two images. If so, it''s convincing and definitely portrays a sense of movement and business.</td>', 'My guess is that this is a composite of at least two images. If so, it''s convincing and definitely portrays a sense of movement and business.', '2011-09-17 19:58:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543536, 972901, 125275, '<td valign="top">Neat! Definitely some digital manipulation, but it''s very subtle and well done.</td>', 'Neat! Definitely some digital manipulation, but it''s very subtle and well done.', '2011-09-17 19:58:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543537, 973510, 125275, '<td valign="top">I believe this is a digital composite. I can see slight reflection of the splash on the left side under the wing, but I don''t see a reflection of the bird''s wing! The resolution/clarity of the water and bird''s wings also seems to be slightly different. Still, it''s pretty convincing.</td>', 'I believe this is a digital composite. I can see slight reflection of the splash on the left side under the wing, but I don''t see a reflection of the bird''s wing! The resolution/clarity of the water and bird''s wings also seems to be slightly different. Still, it''s pretty convincing.', '2011-09-17 19:58:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543539, 973519, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real. Boat would have cast some sort of shadow I think, even in this low light situation. Some stars with trails, some not?</td>', 'Not real. Boat would have cast some sort of shadow I think, even in this low light situation. Some stars with trails, some not?', '2011-09-17 19:58:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543542, 973589, 125275, '<td valign="top">The shadows on the upper child look a bit harsh compared to the shadows on the rest of the image. Plus the direction of that light indicates a flash and the flash would have to be really high (above him) to cast that light, leading me to believe his picture was captured while he was lower in the camera frame and he was later digitally moved. The lower boy''s left arm also looks pasted against that background.<br/> <br/>I also believe if that ninja turtle really existed he would have stopped those two boys from fighting. Really..what is that turtle thing?? :-D <br/> <br/>Final verdict: ''shopped.</td>', 'The shadows on the upper child look a bit harsh compared to the shadows on the rest of the image. Plus the direction of that light indicates a flash and the flash would have to be really high (above him) to cast that light, leading me to believe his picture was captured while he was lower in the camera frame and he was later digitally moved. The lower boy''s left arm also looks pasted against that background. I also believe if that ninja turtle really existed he would have stopped those two boys from fighting. Really..what is that turtle thing?? :-D  Final verdict: ''shopped.', '2011-09-17 19:59:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543543, 973457, 18197, '<td valign="top">Good enough to be real. Like most everything here.</td>', 'Good enough to be real. Like most everything here.', '2011-09-17 19:59:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543544, 973585, 125275, '<td valign="top">I can''t tell if those are jpg artifacts around that bee or remnants of digital compositing. I''m thrown off because of the blurring either. It looks like a blur filter, but the fur is either painstakingly masked out, or it''s just shot with a really wide aperture (which I have no experience doing). It''s just that the feathers in the mouth look *very* blurry compared to the feather below the cat''s face that seem to be the same distance away.<br/>I''m going to guess digitally manufactured, but I mainly feel safe in saying that because I think the bee was added later (at least!)<br/>Looking forward to an answer after the challenge!</td>', 'I can''t tell if those are jpg artifacts around that bee or remnants of digital compositing. I''m thrown off because of the blurring either. It looks like a blur filter, but the fur is either painstakingly masked out, or it''s just shot with a really wide aperture (which I have no experience doing). It''s just that the feathers in the mouth look *very* blurry compared to the feather below the cat''s face that seem to be the same distance away.I''m going to guess digitally manufactured, but I mainly feel safe in saying that because I think the bee was added later (at least!)Looking forward to an answer after the challenge!', '2011-09-17 19:59:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543545, 973613, 125275, '<td valign="top">I think there is a lot of compositing going on here. The color temperature on the guy on the far left doesn''t seem to match the rest of the picture; and his neck seems to have some sort of shadowy growth on it (leftover background). There are interesting highlights around the feet of the blue-shirt-camera-guy. The prophet''s left arm is slightly see through. The police officer looks like he''s in different lighting. Captain America''s sign seems to be missing a contact shadow on the ground. And the middle guy in the black shirt looks too friendly and interesting to be from NYC (kidding on that). Also, the two women posing are posing for...who?<br/> <br/>I''m probably wrong on most of this stuff, but this is what I see. Still, I bet this picture took some time!</td>', 'I think there is a lot of compositing going on here. The color temperature on the guy on the far left doesn''t seem to match the rest of the picture; and his neck seems to have some sort of shadowy growth on it (leftover background). There are interesting highlights around the feet of the blue-shirt-camera-guy. The prophet''s left arm is slightly see through. The police officer looks like he''s in different lighting. Captain America''s sign seems to be missing a contact shadow on the ground. And the middle guy in the black shirt looks too friendly and interesting to be from NYC (kidding on that). Also, the two women posing are posing for...who? I''m probably wrong on most of this stuff, but this is what I see. Still, I bet this picture took some time!', '2011-09-17 20:00:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543546, 973476, 125275, '<td valign="top">This is a very good execution of the challenge. This could very easily go either way and it''s hard to guess which it is. My guess is that it''s a model. My guess is that you shot the model separately from the bottle under the same lighting conditions then composited the two images. The car looks like a model to me because of the reflections and the curves of the car don''t look like they would on a full size model. Besides, you''d need a pretty big white sheet to photograph it on!</td>', 'This is a very good execution of the challenge. This could very easily go either way and it''s hard to guess which it is. My guess is that it''s a model. My guess is that you shot the model separately from the bottle under the same lighting conditions then composited the two images. The car looks like a model to me because of the reflections and the curves of the car don''t look like they would on a full size model. Besides, you''d need a pretty big white sheet to photograph it on!', '2011-09-17 20:00:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543547, 973602, 125275, '<td valign="top">This is a very cool picture and I like the effects. I do believe that is a real boy and a real ocean and a real stick and a real...ok you get the idea. I love the burned edges and texture of this.</td>', 'This is a very cool picture and I like the effects. I do believe that is a real boy and a real ocean and a real stick and a real...ok you get the idea. I love the burned edges and texture of this.', '2011-09-17 20:00:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543548, 973510, 18197, '<td valign="top">May be real, but feels off - sharp water, blurred wings.</td>', 'May be real, but feels off - sharp water, blurred wings.', '2011-09-17 20:00:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543549, 973555, 125275, '<td valign="top">Very interesting! I see a shadow under his hand and index finger that indicates the light is directly in front of him, while on the middle model, the light seems to be coming from her right side. Because of the highlights on her left shoulder that don''t seem to be present in the foremost model, I think those are two different shots. Overall verdict: digitally composited. Still, this is well done and tells a very interesting story.</td>', 'Very interesting! I see a shadow under his hand and index finger that indicates the light is directly in front of him, while on the middle model, the light seems to be coming from her right side. Because of the highlights on her left shoulder that don''t seem to be present in the foremost model, I think those are two different shots. Overall verdict: digitally composited. Still, this is well done and tells a very interesting story.', '2011-09-17 20:01:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543550, 973116, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real but nicely done. Like the elements you chose and how you put them together.</td>', 'Not real but nicely done. Like the elements you chose and how you put them together.', '2011-09-17 20:01:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543551, 973606, 125275, '<td valign="top">I think the patterns of leaves inside this object look like they were manipulated by some sort of photoshop filter. That however, may be an illusion. There doesn''t seem to be enough detail for me to tell! My final answer is: digital manipulation. (But this one''s tough.)</td>', 'I think the patterns of leaves inside this object look like they were manipulated by some sort of photoshop filter. That however, may be an illusion. There doesn''t seem to be enough detail for me to tell! My final answer is: digital manipulation. (But this one''s tough.)', '2011-09-17 20:01:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543552, 973424, 125275, '<td valign="top">This is very interesting. I love the beam of light and how it draws the eye to the bird. The subtleties are nice here as well, the blood, the tic marks on the wall. I do see indications that this is digitally composited, mainly in the shadows (the light coming in the window does not cast shadows), the hair (it''s hard to mask hair, especially the ends), and tic marks appear to be floating slightly. Still, this is a well done image and should finish well!</td>', 'This is very interesting. I love the beam of light and how it draws the eye to the bird. The subtleties are nice here as well, the blood, the tic marks on the wall. I do see indications that this is digitally composited, mainly in the shadows (the light coming in the window does not cast shadows), the hair (it''s hard to mask hair, especially the ends), and tic marks appear to be floating slightly. Still, this is a well done image and should finish well!', '2011-09-17 20:01:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543553, 973392, 125275, '<td valign="top">Definitely real. Nice high key, although on my other monitor all I could see is a face, I couldn''t see the outline of your head.</td>', 'Definitely real. Nice high key, although on my other monitor all I could see is a face, I couldn''t see the outline of your head.', '2011-09-17 20:02:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543554, 973585, 18197, '<td valign="top">Not real ... was the bug added? If it is real - Wow!</td>', 'Not real ... was the bug added? If it is real - Wow!', '2011-09-17 20:02:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543555, 972671, 125275, '<td valign="top">Based on the shadows on her face, I am going to guess this light was added in post-processing. I really like the way you processed the eyes. It''s cool. I might suggest however, if you are going to process the eyes like that, that you might also soften or de-noise the skin. The combination of the processed eyes and unprocessed skin makes the skin look a bit more varied than it probably really is. Oh, I also really like the hair in this shot too.</td>', 'Based on the shadows on her face, I am going to guess this light was added in post-processing. I really like the way you processed the eyes. It''s cool. I might suggest however, if you are going to process the eyes like that, that you might also soften or de-noise the skin. The combination of the processed eyes and unprocessed skin makes the skin look a bit more varied than it probably really is. Oh, I also really like the hair in this shot too.', '2011-09-17 20:02:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6543556, 973583, 18197, '<td valign="top">Probably real.</td>', 'Probably real.', '2011-09-17 20:02:32.000000', NULL, 1),
