(6547176, 973597, 88850, '<td valign="top">Great idea.  Well executed.  (not voting)</td>', 'Great idea.  Well executed.  (not voting)', '2011-09-21 12:38:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6547288, 973286, 125275, '<td valign="top">Interesting. To my eye, the mirrors seem to be refracting at different strengths, indicating to me that this is some sort of digital composite. There is, however, reflected light that seems to be cast pretty uniformly over the mirrors and that seems to be coming from whatever pink light source is close by. While looking on the inside of the mirror (at the boundary of what would be glass and plasic), it looks like the image has a harsh transition, i.e. unnatural. Almost as if the reflected images were overlayed and masked. Final verdict: digitally manufactured.<br/> <br/>***<br/>I''m going to guess that I got this wrong. I''m interested in seeing how it was done...is it just an illusion?</td>', 'Interesting. To my eye, the mirrors seem to be refracting at different strengths, indicating to me that this is some sort of digital composite. There is, however, reflected light that seems to be cast pretty uniformly over the mirrors and that seems to be coming from whatever pink light source is close by. While looking on the inside of the mirror (at the boundary of what would be glass and plasic), it looks like the image has a harsh transition, i.e. unnatural. Almost as if the reflected images were overlayed and masked. Final verdict: digitally manufactured. ***I''m going to guess that I got this wrong. I''m interested in seeing how it was done...is it just an illusion?', '2011-09-21 15:23:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6547312, 973457, 137320, '<td valign="top">This technically may not be much, but it speaks to me. So few artists can connect with the viewer and achieve the intended impact of their work. Well done.</td>', 'This technically may not be much, but it speaks to me. So few artists can connect with the viewer and achieve the intended impact of their work. Well done.', '2011-09-21 16:01:18.000000', NULL, 1),
