(6559908, 973295, 30364, '<td valign="top">Alexander Bayliss, as a young man.<br/> <br/>If you haven''t read <a href="//www.goodreads.com/book/show/194638.The_Industry_of_Souls" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">The Industry of Souls</a> then may I give you the urge?  Martin Booth is dead now, but I think you''d nominate the novel for the posthumous blue.</td>', 'Alexander Bayliss, as a young man. If you haven''t read The Industry of Souls then may I give you the urge?  Martin Booth is dead now, but I think you''d nominate the novel for the posthumous blue.', '2011-10-04 06:47:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6562364, 972671, 93565, '<td valign="top">I saw you post in the forum about feedback-<br/>It''s a well lit portrait, and interesting, to boot. The eyes are have a lot of allure, but are perhaps a bit overdone, in my opinion. The lighting on the hair is very nice and gives a good flow and texture to things. I''d like to see her shoulders moved in a bit of a manner so she doesn''t quite look armless. I know you''re obviously limited in that you presumably didn''t want to show nudity, but angling raising the arms a bit or something would suffice.<br/>Overall though, I think the biggest drawback is just that it wasn''t entirely clear what we were supposed to be fooled by. Regardless of how you accomplished this, there are ways to do it both in PS and in camera. On the bright side, though, your shot made me think of <a href="//www.zarias.com/gulf-photo-plus-my-shootout-with-david-hobby-joey-l/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a> so consider yourself in excellent company :)</td>', 'I saw you post in the forum about feedback-It''s a well lit portrait, and interesting, to boot. The eyes are have a lot of allure, but are perhaps a bit overdone, in my opinion. The lighting on the hair is very nice and gives a good flow and texture to things. I''d like to see her shoulders moved in a bit of a manner so she doesn''t quite look armless. I know you''re obviously limited in that you presumably didn''t want to show nudity, but angling raising the arms a bit or something would suffice.Overall though, I think the biggest drawback is just that it wasn''t entirely clear what we were supposed to be fooled by. Regardless of how you accomplished this, there are ways to do it both in PS and in camera. On the bright side, though, your shot made me think of this so consider yourself in excellent company :)', '2011-10-06 14:20:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(6566061, 973509, 12611, '<td valign="top">Shots like this do such a great service to the era of photo-shop and post processing. After reading how much work you put into it, it really paid off, not in a fantastical fantasy sort of way- but an easy- perfectly believable and well done way. This and all your shots are works to aspire to. (gushing flattery session over.)</td>', 'Shots like this do such a great service to the era of photo-shop and post processing. After reading how much work you put into it, it really paid off, not in a fantastical fantasy sort of way- but an easy- perfectly believable and well done way. This and all your shots are works to aspire to. (gushing flattery session over.)', '2011-10-11 09:57:36.000000', NULL, 0),
